EXPERIMENTAL / UNTESTED - DO NOT MERGE INTO A DEFAULT KERNEL
FP6 network feature push, 2026-10-24.

wifi: ath11k: advertise P2P interface modes for WCN6750 (FP6 Wi-Fi Display probe)

Purpose: the only prerequisite for Miracast (Wi-Fi Display over Wi-Fi Direct)
is a P2P-capable wiphy. Pinned ath11k advertises P2P_DEVICE/CLIENT/GO for
QCA6390, WCN6855, QCA2066 and QCA6698AQ, but only STATION|AP for WCN6750
(FP6 reports qcom,wcn6755-wifi with a wcn6750 fallback). The P2P code paths in
mac.c (vdev subtypes, GO beacon P2P IE, combination limits) are chip-generic
and keyed off this mask. With this change ath11k_mac_setup_iface_combinations()
adds P2P_CLIENT/GO to the AP limit and a P2P_DEVICE limit (max 1); hw_params
num_vdevs=3 still bounds STA + P2P-device + GO.

Unknown, therefore experimental: whether WLAN.MSL.3.0.1-00328.3 firmware on
WPSS implements the P2P vdev subtypes, NoA and remain-on-channel for this
chip; upstream never enabled it. Validate only on a RAM-booted test kernel
(fastboot boot, never flash), and check `iw phy` shows P2P modes,
`iw dev wlan0 interface add p2p-dev0 type __p2pdev` succeeds, STA traffic on
wlan0 is unaffected, and there are no ath11k firmware crashes/recovery in
dmesg. If firmware asserts, drop this patch: Miracast is then not feasible on
the mainline transport. Building/testing is left to the kernel agent; this
feature push built no kernel.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.c
@@ -614,7 +614,10 @@
 		},
 
 		.interface_modes = BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION) |
-					BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP),
+					BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_AP) |
+					BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_DEVICE) |
+					BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_CLIENT) |
+					BIT(NL80211_IFTYPE_P2P_GO),
 		.supports_monitor = false,
 		.supports_shadow_regs = true,
 		.idle_ps = true,
